This report outlines the setup, configuration and execution of the Hyperledger Fabric FabCar network on an Ubuntu 24.04.2 system. The process includes installing prerequisites, setting up the Fabric environment, launching the test network, and interacting with the FabCar application using JavaScript for asset management.

-------------------------------------------------------------

1. Environment Setup
-------------------

1.1 Install Prerequisites
To prepare the system for Hyperledger Fabric, essential tools were installed using the following command on an Ubuntu 24.04.2 system:

    sudo apt install curl git docker.io docker-compose golang make jq -y

Tools Installed:
- curl: For downloading files.
- git: For version control.
- docker.io and docker-compose: For running the network in containers.
- golang: For Go programming (used in chaincode).
- make: For building software.
- jq: For handling JSON data.

1.2 Configure Docker
Docker was configured to run the blockchain network in containers. The following commands were executed to enable and start the Docker service and add the user to the Docker group for non-root access:

    sudo systemctl enable docker
    sudo systemctl start docker
    sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

1.3 Install Go
Go was installed to support chaincode development, and the environment was configured to include Go in the system path:

    sudo apt update && sudo apt install golang-go -y
    echo 'export PATH=$PATH:/usr/lib/go/bin' >> ~/.bashrc
    source ~/.bashrc

Verification:
    go version

Output:
    go version go1.22.2 linux/amd64

